<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/2nd-century-bce">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Siege</p><h1 class="enc-title">Siege of Carthage (149–146 BCE)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/146-bce">146 BCE</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/2nd-century-bce">2nd century BCE</a> · Also known as systematically demolished Carthage · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/third-punic-war">Third Punic War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Siege of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carthage">Carthage</a> was the main engagement of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/third-punic-war">Third Punic War</a>, in which Roman forces besieged the city of Carthage. In 146 BCE <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scipio-aemilianus">Scipio Aemilianus</a> took the city, which was systematically demolished and its population killed or enslaved. Accounts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/punic-empire">Punic Empire</a> treat this as the end of Carthage.</p></div>
